<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 669 0 R/E(Transnational Organized Crime \(TOC\): Criminal activities carried out by organized groups that operate across national borders.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

228 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 670 0 R/E(Suspicious Transaction Report \(STR\): A report submitted by financial institutions when a transaction or activity is suspected to involve illicit funds.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

229 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 671 0 R/E(Know Your Customer \(KYC\): Procedures used by financial institutions to verify customers and assess potential financial risks.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

230 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 672 0 R/E(Customer Due Diligence \(CDD\): Measures taken to identify customers, understand their financial activities, and assess associated risks.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

231 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 673 0 R/E(Beneficial Owner: The individual who ultimately owns or controls a company, account, or financial asset, even if it is held through another person or entity.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

232 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 674 0 R/E(Illicit Financial Flows \(IFFs\): Money transferred across borders through illegal activities, such as corruption, trafficking, tax evasion, or terrorist financing.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

233 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 675 0 R/E(Asset Freezing: The legal restriction preventing individuals or entities from accessing, transferring, or disposing of their financial assets.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

234 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 676 0 R/E(Financial Sanctions: Restrictions imposed on individuals, organizations, or entities to limit or prohibit their access to financial resources.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

235 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 677 0 R/E(Red Flag Indicators: Warning signs or unusual patterns in financial activity that may indicate money laundering, terrorist financing, or other criminal activity.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

236 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 678 0 R/E(Information Sharing: The exchange of financial intelligence between FIUs, law-enforcement agencies, and international partners to identify and disrupt illicit networks.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

237 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 679 0 R/E(Risk-Based Approach \(RBA\): A strategy in which financial institutions and authorities allocate greater resources to areas presenting higher risks of financial crime.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

238 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 680 0 R/E(Virtual Assets: Digital representations of value, such as cryptocurrencies, that can be transferred or traded electronically and may be exploited for illicit financial activities.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

