458 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 141 0 R/E(UNTOC and the Terrorist Financing Convention set the international obligations, but they are implemented through a wide range of differently designed national laws, and the specific mechanics of those laws determine what a resolution can realistically ask states to change. Delegates who can cite how a bloc's own legal system actually works are far more persuasive than delegates who only cite the treaty.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

459 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 722 0 R/E(United States: the Bank Secrecy Act \(1970\) established the core reporting framework, later strengthened by the USA PATRIOT Act \(2001\), whose Title III specifically targets international money laundering and terrorist financing, and further updated by the Anti-Money Laundering Act of 2020 \(in force from January 2021\), the first major modernization of the BSA in two decades.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

460 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 723 0 R/E(United Kingdom: the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 \(POCA\) provides the core confiscation and civil-recovery powers, supplemented by the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds Regulations 2017 and the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act 2018 \(royal assent 23 May 2018\), which gave the UK independent sanctions-making power after leaving the EU framework.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

461 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 724 0 R/E(European Union: the Anti-Money Laundering Directives set minimum standards across all member states; the Fourth Directive \(4AMLD, 2015\) required compliance by June 2017, and the Fifth and Sixth Directives \(5AMLD/6AMLD\) took effect from January 2020, progressively expanding beneficial-ownership transparency and criminal-liability rules.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

462 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 725 0 R/E(India: the Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002 \(enacted January 2003, in force from July 2005\) is implemented by FIU-IND under the Ministry of Finance and has been amended repeatedly, most recently to widen the reporting regime to additional business categories.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

463 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 726 0 R/E(South Africa: the Financial Intelligence Centre Act, 2001 \(FICA\) is the core statute, amended in 2022 through the General Laws \(Anti-Money Laundering and Combating Terrorism Financing\) Amendment Act to correct deficiencies identified in FATF's 2021 mutual evaluation of the country.)/Pg 23 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

464 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 141 0 R/T(Legal Frameworks, Sanctions & Asset Recovery)/E(Legal Frameworks, Sanctions & Asset Recovery)/Pg 23 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

