491 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 142 0 R/T(THE WAY FORWARD)/E(THE WAY FORWARD)/Pg 24 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

492 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 142 0 R/E(Delegates are encouraged to approach the agenda with a focus on practical, cooperative, and sustainable solutions to combat terrorist financing and transnational organized crime. Discussions should prioritize strengthening Financial Intelligence Units \(FIUs\), improving real-time information sharing, enhancing cross-border cooperation, and developing stronger mechanisms to trace, freeze, and recover illicit assets. Delegates should also consider emerging challenges such as cryptocurrencies, digital financial systems, shell companies, and informal money-transfer networks, while ensuring that proposed measures respect national sovereignty, privacy, and human rights. Ultimately, the committee should work toward a coordinated international framework that enables states to identify illicit financial flows early, disrupt criminal networks, and prevent financial systems from being exploited for terrorism and organized crime.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

